WEBVTT

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:11.530
Yes.

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:13.450
I found it.

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:16.700
He's on the phone again.
Is it Mr. Hanekoma?

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.210
Thanks.

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:25.000
I'm counting on you, Mr. Hanekoma.
You really know Shibuya.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Why would he work with
someone like Joshua?

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.340
Does Mr. Hanekoma know
that this guy killed me?

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.550
Hi there, Neku.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:35.260
Sweet dreams?

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.640
The worst.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.230
"The World Ends With You The Animation"

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:13.150
Joshua

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:13.070
How can you act so casual?!

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:16.950
Well, we <i>are </i>partners.

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:23.210
If you erased me, you'd be done for too.

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:29.840
The Reapers' Game and
missions don't matter to you.

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.260
You're just out for yourself!

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:35.260
Because unlike me, you're alive!

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:37.300
That's not true, Neku.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:40.510
It is true! You won't get erased!

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:44.600
A mission?!

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:50.900
"Beat the bosses of 2.2360679's 0 and 5.

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:53.070
You have 60 minutes."

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:57.990
I'm playing by the same rules
as the rest of you.

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:00.120
If I'm erased in the Underground,

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.870
I'll be erased in the Realground too.

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:04.710
What?

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:09.080
You came to the Underground
even though you might die?

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:13.130
It beats being in the Realground.

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:19.640
So, Minamimoto was behind the Taboo Noise?

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:22.060
This is a serious act of treason.

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:26.310
I'll discuss Minamimoto's
punishment with the Composer.

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:28.900
I request a swift resolution.

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:32.400
By the way,

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:37.280
a second-time Player, Neku Sakuraba,
is proving exceptionally long-lived.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.990
What do you think of that , sir?

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:44.330
So, that's how it is.

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:46.660
The composer has a mischievous streak.

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:50.790
The bosses of 0 and 5...

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:53.880
What's 2.2360679?

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:56.220
Some kind of code?

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:58.180
I've got a guess.

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:22.200
I hope this hits.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.960
OK, Neku, let's keep going.

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:36.380
Center Street

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:42.760
I thought so. Only Route 5 is open today.

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:44.970
How'd you know?

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:50.060
2.2360679 is the square root of 5.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:52.690
There's even a mnemonic for it.

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:55.980
Damn it! He's screwing with us.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:59.320
Route 5 runs starts at Scramble Crossing

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:06.950
and runs through Center Street, AMX,
Tipsy Tose Hall, Tokyu Hands, and Udagawa.

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:10.370
Then the bosses of 0+5...

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:14.540
...are in Scramble Crossing and...
One, two...

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:15.790
Udagawa!

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:16.840
You got it.

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:18.960
We just beat the first boss,

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:23.050
so if we beat the boss of Udagawa,
we clear the mission.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:26.600
Damn it!

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:29.850
There's a lot of tough Noise today!

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:33.270
Broadly speaking,
there are two types of Noise.

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:38.400
Stray Noise is the natural product of
negative human emotion in the Realground.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:42.490
Stray Noise obeys Reapers
and attacks Players.

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:45.070
And these are the other type?!

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:49.330
That Reaper, Kariya,
called them Taboo Noise.

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:53.920
They attack Players and Reapers
regardless of missions.

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:55.880
I can't afford to lose!

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:00.590
We did it, Nao!

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:02.130
Nao! Nao!

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:09.560
Looks like I've had it.

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:12.810
Sorry, So--

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:14.190
Nao!

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:16.440
Nao's gone.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:20.980
God damn it!

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:23.030
Sorry.

00:06:23.030 --> 00:06:24.610
You guys...

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:27.320
If we'd gotten here a little sooner...

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:30.330
H-Hey!

00:06:32.290 --> 00:06:35.420
Stick it out to the end.

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:38.460
Get back the partner
they made your entry fee.

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:41.260
You've gotta come back... to life.

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:43.670
Shit!

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:48.220
Again. Before my eyes.

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:50.720
But we're still alive.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:53.270
What's happens to the ones who aren't?!

00:06:56.850 --> 00:07:00.610
I know we Players are
strangers to each other.

00:07:00.610 --> 00:07:05.240
And not just Players. Everyone on
the street's a stranger too.

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:09.030
They all have different values
and ways of thinking.

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:11.120
But I...

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:14.710
I met a lot of people
in Shibuya, and I felt it.

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:18.580
I felt my world grow, just a little.

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:22.130
So, I don't want to just shut them out!

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:26.550
That's not like you, Neku,

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:31.470
but it's because you interacted with
others than you can find a new you.

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:33.560
Is that the gist of it?

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:34.680
Let's hurry.

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:37.770
We'll have to clear the mission ourselves.

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:51.530
Uzuki!

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:55.500
You OK?

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:57.540
There's too many of them.

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:00.500
The Game Master must be
mass producing them.

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:06.130
Those two!

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:08.510
What shall we do, Neku?

00:08:08.510 --> 00:08:11.680
I don't want to watch someone die.

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:13.720
We'll back them up!

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:34.160
That just leaves these guys!

00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:39.240
OK!

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:40.170
Hey!

00:08:40.170 --> 00:08:41.920
What do you think you're doing?!

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:47.420
What? You'd rather we didn't save you?

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:52.180
We're Reapers! Your enemies, remember?

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:56.390
Anyway, I can take care of my--

00:08:56.390 --> 00:08:57.680
Whoa there.

00:08:57.680 --> 00:08:59.440
Don't overdo it.

00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:01.600
Thanks. You saved us.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:03.730
Hey! What are you talking about?!

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:05.770
Can't forget to say thanks.

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:10.990
Players saving Reapers?! What a pain!

00:09:10.990 --> 00:09:12.530
Let's go, Kariya!

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:21.040
The Game Master's not
gonna play by the rules.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:24.460
This won't be like last time. Watch out.

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:27.370
Udagawa

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:29.800
How's the time?

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:31.840
Thirty minutes left.

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:33.050
That's plenty.

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:43.520
That's the boss.

00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:46.820
Be careful, Neku!

00:09:46.820 --> 00:09:48.320
Got it. Let's go!

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:55.030
Fighting up close is risky! Get back!

00:10:00.330 --> 00:10:01.750
Another one.

00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:03.460
Huh?

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:04.830
Watch out!

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:07.500
Wow. It's surprisingly nimble.

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:22.850
Bye-bye!

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:35.570
Mission clear, huh?

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:37.120
One more day.

00:10:38.410 --> 00:10:40.660
Hang on, Shiki.

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:45.580
This is zetta thrilling.

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:52.260
What do you want today?

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:55.550
You guys getting erased
would throw off my plans.

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:57.340
Tomorrow's day seven.

00:10:57.340 --> 00:11:01.100
They special day I get
to take you on myself.

00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:04.180
Now, time for a question.

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:07.520
How fast am I gonna erase you two?

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:08.900
No clue.

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:13.240
299,729,458 m/s.

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:15.820
Would that be the speed of light?

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:19.990
I'm gonna solve the calculation
I screwed up here that day!

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:27.330
It's finally the last day.

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:30.130
My second Reapers' Game ends today.

00:11:34.590 --> 00:11:36.180
That's right.

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:46.230
That hurts.

00:11:46.230 --> 00:11:47.980
Promise me.

00:11:47.980 --> 00:11:51.860
After today's mission,
I'll make you tell me everything.

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:55.030
I suppose.

00:11:58.990 --> 00:12:02.410
"Defeat the Game Master at Mark City.

00:12:02.410 --> 00:12:05.290
Incompletes will be erased," huh?

00:12:05.290 --> 00:12:07.870
It's a good spot for a base.

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:09.790
Why's that?

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:12.290
All the emotion in Shibuya collects here.

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:16.800
It crashes into Mark City
and shoots up into the sky.

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:21.800
That emotion flows back down
and keeps building up here.

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:25.770
If we can beat him,

00:12:25.770 --> 00:12:27.890
it'll all be over.

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:30.100
Hold on, Shiki.

00:12:33.650 --> 00:12:35.650
This looks like the only way in.

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:46.870
It's too dark to see clearly.

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:51.420
Watch your step. I wouldn't
want my partner getting hurt.

00:12:51.420 --> 00:12:53.670
Mind your own business.

00:12:53.670 --> 00:12:55.590
Get your head in the game!

00:12:56.800 --> 00:12:57.970
Noise!

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:06.140
Damn it!

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:10.600
It's so dark, I can't tell
where they're attacking from!

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:12.060
I can't get close!

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:18.110
The lights...

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:19.320
There!

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:32.620
Today's the day I take you down!

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:39.590
I switched on the emergency lights.

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:42.430
That makes us even for before.

00:13:42.430 --> 00:13:47.260
Good grief. How awkward can Skater Boy be?

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:50.930
Is his "special op" for Mr. Kitaniji
to pretend to pick fights

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:54.810
and protect those boys
from Noise and Reapers?

00:13:56.440 --> 00:13:59.280
I've got no clue what's
even right anymore.

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:04.780
What's going on?!

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:06.080
Isn't this weird?!

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:09.790
Space is warping!

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:16.420
It might be the imaginary number plane.

00:14:16.420 --> 00:14:18.420
The imaginary what now?

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:22.130
A parallel world an infinitesimal distance
from the one Noise inhabits.

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:25.220
That might be where we're fighting.

00:14:27.180 --> 00:14:28.600
Dodge, Beat!

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:33.850
It might be risky to stay too long.

00:14:42.530 --> 00:14:44.110
Here.

00:14:44.110 --> 00:14:45.570
You dropped this.

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:53.540
I owe you one.

00:15:06.430 --> 00:15:07.550
Again?!

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:09.560
Did Minamimoto do this?

00:15:11.770 --> 00:15:14.390
This <i>is </i>his base, after all.

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:16.230
We can't get careless.

00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:26.280
What're you guys doing here?!

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:28.990
Could it be an inverse matrix?!

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:30.740
A what?

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:33.950
Forget it. You saved me a trip.

00:15:36.170 --> 00:15:41.500
But I was hoping to set up the same
situation in the same place as that time.

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:43.170
"That time"?

00:15:44.260 --> 00:15:46.090
Yes, that time.

00:16:18.670 --> 00:16:19.960
Neku?

00:16:21.170 --> 00:16:23.300
So,<i> you </i>killed me,

00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:24.710
Minamimoto!

00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:28.300
Come and get it!

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:31.430
I'm gonna eliminate you
from my spatial coordinates!

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:41.310
Drown in the sea... of imaginary numbers!

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:51.660
Look, Neku!

00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:56.870
Taboo Noise!

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:58.620
And so many of them!

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:03.130
He's been using the Shibuya's emotional
energy that pools at Mark City

00:17:03.130 --> 00:17:05.420
to manufacture Taboo Noise.

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:18.560
Be careful!

00:17:18.560 --> 00:17:20.020
Right back at you.

00:17:24.730 --> 00:17:25.770
What?!

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:27.150
Tera slow!

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:30.150
Neku!

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:37.080
You're zetta slow!

00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:49.130
Get down!

00:17:55.350 --> 00:17:57.060
This is nothing!

00:18:02.690 --> 00:18:04.060
Don't get cocky!

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:20.200
He's way stronger than
everything else so far.

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:24.670
I'm on another level!

00:18:26.090 --> 00:18:27.420
This is bad.

00:18:29.050 --> 00:18:30.710
We're just getting started.

00:18:34.680 --> 00:18:38.430
I've never gotten so much
power from this guy before.

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:42.940
With this, we can win!

00:18:42.940 --> 00:18:44.770
I'll draw him out.

00:19:16.930 --> 00:19:18.640
You're zetta tough.

00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:22.720
You might be the one who gets erased.

00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:30.440
What?

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:33.990
Did you know?!
The world's made of numbers!

00:19:33.990 --> 00:19:38.280
I've been reverse-engineering
my desired solution all this time!

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:40.410
And this...

00:19:40.410 --> 00:19:45.410
...is my answer!

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:47.330
This is...!

00:19:53.260 --> 00:19:54.470
What the...?

00:19:59.430 --> 00:20:01.890
You can't afford to lose, right, Neku?

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:07.390
You'll survive and make
your wish come true.

00:20:12.650 --> 00:20:14.400
Why?

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:16.280
Why did you cover for me?

00:20:17.450 --> 00:20:21.330
I always suspected you, so why did you...?

00:20:22.410 --> 00:20:24.870
Joshua!

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:33.800
You're...

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:35.170
Congratulations.

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:40.760
You did well to survive again,
and thank you for cooperating with us.

00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:43.010
I don't remember helping you.

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:45.560
You dealt with the rebel.

00:20:45.560 --> 00:20:49.060
I sent the final mission myself.

00:20:49.060 --> 00:20:55.110
Minamimoto unleashed Taboo Noise and
killed many Reapers. You dealt with him.

00:20:55.110 --> 00:20:57.320
Thank you.

00:20:57.320 --> 00:20:59.910
You used us?

00:20:59.910 --> 00:21:05.950
I'm sorry about your partner.
I never expected him to shield you.

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:07.960
Is Joshua...?

00:21:07.960 --> 00:21:12.290
He was erased along
with Minamimoto, as you saw.

00:21:12.290 --> 00:21:14.460
I haven't apologized yet.

00:21:14.460 --> 00:21:18.420
I haven't apologized to him, to Joshua.

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:23.430
He was my partner, but I could
never bring myself to trust him.

00:21:23.430 --> 00:21:25.930
I'm the worst.

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:28.020
No need to grieve.

00:21:28.020 --> 00:21:31.650
He committed a serious offense.

00:21:31.650 --> 00:21:33.480
You mean being alive?

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:37.650
And he gave you your next ordeal.

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:40.650
As his partner, you share his
guilt for breaking the rules.

00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:42.530
You will be erased.

00:21:43.700 --> 00:21:48.500
But considering the extent
of your service to us,

00:21:48.500 --> 00:21:52.210
I will permit you to enter a third game,
albeit with a penalty.

00:21:52.210 --> 00:21:54.130
You cannot refuse.

00:21:54.130 --> 00:21:57.710
And Shiki? What about Shiki?

00:21:57.710 --> 00:22:03.260
Your penalty is disqualification
from all future games.

00:22:03.260 --> 00:22:07.390
As far as you're concerned,
the next game is the last.

00:22:07.390 --> 00:22:10.430
The next game is the last?

00:22:10.430 --> 00:22:13.690
Now, as for your third entry fee...

00:22:19.940 --> 00:22:22.280
Here I go again.

00:22:24.280 --> 00:22:25.910
This is...

00:22:25.910 --> 00:22:27.740
...my last game.

00:23:58.950 --> 00:24:01.960
Emergency Call

00:23:59.380 --> 00:24:01.800
Next time: "Emergency Call."
